  "description_short": "Forest-edge lodge dining with spa comforts near Tsitsikamma's ancient yellowwoods and adventure trails.",
  "description_long": "Tsitsikhaya Lodge Restaurant brings honest country cooking to the doorstep of Storms River's indigenous forests. The dining room overlooks indigenous gardens where Cape sugarbirds flit between proteas, and meals lean toward hearty South African comfort food that fuels hikers and travellers exploring Tsitsikamma's canopy tours and coastal paths.\n\nThe kitchen keeps things simple and satisfying—grills, linefish when available, and vegetarian options that make use of seasonal produce. After a day on the Otter Trail or swinging through the forest canopy, the restaurant's unhurried pace and warm atmosphere feel exactly right. The on-site spa adds another layer of recovery for adventure-weary guests.\n\nLocation-wise, you're perfectly positioned between Plettenberg Bay and Port Elizabeth, with the dramatic Storms River Mouth and ancient yellowwood forests minutes away. It's a practical, comfortable base where the focus stays on good food, genuine hospitality, and the remarkable natural surroundings that make this corner of the Garden Route unforgettable.",
